WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.013
A terminal is enough: Run setup --terminal on a headless server. These are real wizard prompts using tiny synthetic FASTQs.

2
00:00:07.013 --> 00:00:11.873
Choose libraries: The wizard discovers the synthetic FASTQs. Enter all to include every listed library.

3
00:00:11.873 --> 00:00:17.089
Keep the library identity: Press Enter to keep the discovered sample name and its existing FASTQ pair.

4
00:00:17.089 --> 00:00:22.282
Assign the sample type: These tutorial libraries are cancer samples. Choose the type from your own sample records.

5
00:00:22.282 --> 00:00:27.130
Choose copy-number analysis: Enter cna. This walkthrough configures copy-number analysis only.

6
00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:31.754
Set the CPU budget: The wizard reports the current machine. Choose 4 threads here; budget resources for your own server.

7
00:00:31.754 --> 00:00:36.610
Choose Illumina bins: Use QDNAseq at 100 kb for this tutorial. The wizard records the selected resolution.

8
00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:41.350
Keep the example focused: Choose no for additional CNA interpretation reports.

9
00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:46.091
Keep small variants off: Choose no. This CNA-only setup does not request variant or FFPE assessment.

10
00:00:46.091 --> 00:00:51.518
Select reference handling: Choose download for prebuilt hg38 indexes when analysis runs. Saving does not download them.

11
00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:56.259
Choose CPU or GPU: On an NVIDIA GPU server, choose Yes for supported stages or No to use CPU. This walkthrough keeps CPU.

12
00:00:56.259 --> 00:01:05.638
Review and save only: Review the saved configuration and input checks, then explicitly enter save. No analysis starts.

13
00:01:05.638 --> 00:01:14.208
Configuration saved: The wizard confirms: saved without starting analysis. Keep the project and launch the analysis separately when ready.
